 "stimulus_html": "For the following exercises, use the connected graphs. In each exercise, a graph is indicated. Determine if the graph is Eulerian or not and explain how you know. If it is Eulerian, give an example of an Euler circuit. If it is not, state which edge or edges you would duplicate to eulerize the graph.\n<br>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/2513213511b4867a.png\" alt=\"Four graphs. Graph J has 16 vertices. The edges are a b, a c, a d, b e, c d, d e, e f, c g, d h, e i, f j, g h, h i, i j, g k, h m, i n, j o, k m, m n, n o, m p, n q, o q, and p q. Graph K has 12 vertices. The edges are a b, a d, b e, c d, d e, e f, c, d h, e i, f j, g h, h i, i j, h k, i m, and k m. Multigraph L has four vertices. The straight edges are labeled as follows: n q, B; no, D; q p, F; o p, G; q c, C. The curved edges are labeled as follows: q n, A; n o, E; o p, I; p q, H. Graph M has 12 vertices. The edges are labeled a b, a c, a d, b e, b f, c d, d e, e f, c g, g d, d h, h e, e i, i f, f j, g h, h i, i j, g k, h k, i m, j m, and k m.\">\n",
